---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
      <h2 class="h2" id="problem-title">Port 3000 is taken, again. <span class="soft">But ports aren't the whole story.</span></h2>
      <p class="lede">
        You're running Claude Code in one terminal, Cursor in another, Docker on the side, and three
        agents started their own servers. A PID and <code>kill -9</code> don't tell you who owns what —
        or how to stop only the right thing.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="side">
        <div class="term-window">
          <div class="window-bar"><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="window-title">Without portwise</span><span class="pad" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<pre class="term" tabindex="0"><span class="p">$</span> PORT=3000 npm run dev
<span class="r">Error: listen EADDRINUSE: address already in use :::3000</span>
<span class="p">$</span> lsof -i :3000
<span class="d">COMMAND   PID USER   FD   TYPE  NODE NAME</span>
node    43000  dev   23u  IPv6  TCP *:hbci (LISTEN)
<span class="p">$</span> kill -9 43000
<span class="p">$</span> PORT=3000 npm run dev
<span class="r">Error: listen EADDRINUSE: address already in use :::3000</span>
<span class="d"># …the parent respawned it. Which agent started that?</span></pre>
        </div>
        <ul class="notes">
          <li><Icon name="X" size={16} /> No idea which project, agent or tool</li>
          <li><Icon name="X" size={16} /> <code>kill -9</code> skips cleanup</li>
          <li><Icon name="X" size={16} /> No view of what each agent can reach</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="side">
        <div class="term-window">
          <div class="window-bar"><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="window-title">With portwise</span><span class="pad" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<pre class="term" tabindex="0"><span class="p">$</span> portwise agents
<span class="v">Claude Code</span>  pid 51200 · terminal agent · you
  folders   shop-api  ~/code/shop-api
  ports     :3001  shop-api (Vite)  · stoppable
  access    sandbox unknown · network :3001 only
<span class="p">$</span> portwise agents claude --stop-ports --yes
  <span class="d">· sent SIGTERM to npm (51199), node (51201)</span>
<span class="g">✔</span> <span class="b">:3001 is free</span>
<span class="p">$</span> PORT=3000 npm run dev  <span class="g">✓ Ready in 1.4s</span></pre>
        </div>
        <ul class="notes good">
          <li><Icon name="Check" size={16} /> Names the agent, folder and access</li>
          <li><Icon name="Check" size={16} /> Stops only what that agent started</li>
          <li><Icon name="Check" size={16} /> Every fact marked seen, inferred or unknown</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 24px; align-items: start; }
  .side { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  .pad { flex: none; width: 52px; }
  pre { margin: 0; padding: 16px 20px; min-height: 220px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .notes { list-style: none; margin: 20px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 8px; font-size: var(--fs-md); line-height: 24px; color: var(--muted); }
  .notes li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  .notes :global(svg) { flex: none; color: var(--muted); }
  .notes.good { color: var(--text-2); }
  .notes.good :global(svg) { color: var(--accent-text); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .pair { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 40px; } }
</style>
